  "title": "Schur-log-concavity for the complete eight-vertex layer of the multiweighted-bond symmetric function",
  "batch_label": "40",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every connected simple graph G on exactly eight vertices and every integer d >= 1, (Psi_G|degree d)^2 - (Psi_G|degree d-1)(Psi_G|degree d+1) is Schur-positive. More precisely, for d=1,...,7 every Schur coefficient is a positive integer (the minimum over all graphs, degrees, and partitions is 1), while for d>=8 the expression is zero.",
